---
/* The site's contact surface, on every page including /404.
   Decided in issue #34: `mailto:` stays, and a LinkedIn link joins it. No
   contact form — see docs/content-architecture.md §1 for the reasoning and for
   the trigger that would reopen it.

   This is the repo's first component, so it sets the precedent: scoped <style>
   in the file, no token hard-coded, no new type role. */
import { EMAIL, LINKEDIN } from '../site';
---

{/* No data-anim. The footer is on the first screen on /404 and on the current
    placeholder /, and base.css:106 rules first-screen elements out of
    Registration. Independently, CONTEXT.md scopes Registration to information
    arriving — the footer is furniture that is simply present. */}
<footer class="t-spec">
  <a class="address" href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>
  {/* rel="me" pairs with the Person graph's sameAs on /. No target="_blank":
      it decides tab behaviour on the visitor's behalf and drags rel="noopener"
      in behind it. */}
  <a href={LINKEDIN} rel="me">LinkedIn</a>
</footer>

<style>
  /* Aligned to the same 1600px measure and gutter as index.astro's <main>, so
     the footer sits on the page's left edge rather than the viewport's.

     `width: 100%` for the reason spelled out in base.css: <body> is a flex
     column, and `margin-inline: auto` on a flex item beats `align-items:
     stretch`, so without it this shrink-to-fits and centres itself. */
  footer {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px 28px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1600px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: calc(var(--rhythm) * 0.5) var(--gutter);
  }

  /* --muted arrives from .t-spec. It is 4.90:1 on the day ground and 5.01:1 on
     the night ground — computed from the oklab mixes in tokens.css, not eyeballed.
     --t-spec is 0.6875rem = 11px, so the WCAG large-text 3:1 exemption does not
     apply and 4.5:1 is the bar. NEVER --signal here: it is not a text colour. */
  a {
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  /* Same reasoning as the home page's old email line, which this replaces: an
     address is data you read and type, not a phrase set in caps, and
     IME@COULTERHEIBERGER.COM was the least readable actionable string on the site.

     THIS LINE DEPENDS ON THE FONT CUT. MONO_SPEC was uppercase-only, and
     `text-transform: none` against that subset does not lowercase the line, it
     shatters it — `@` and `.` from JetBrains Mono, every letter from Consolas.
     U+0061-007A is in the cut for exactly this line (docs/styling.md#fonts). If
     the mono subset is ever narrowed again, this breaks silently and visibly. */
  .address {
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: normal;
  }
</style>
